# Marathon Librem 5 modem USB autosuspend + wakeup enable.
#
# The Librem 5's BroadMobi BM818 modem presents as a USB device
# (Qualcomm-licensed MSM bridge — vendor 2020 product 2060) on the
# i.MX 8MQ's xhci-hcd. By default the kernel sets `wakeup: disabled`
# on this device, which is fatal for power: the runtime suspend path
# requires a usable wake source, so a wakeup-disabled device CANNOT
# enter runtime_suspended. Result: USB polls run continuously, ~36
# interrupts/sec on xhci-hcd:usb1, and the modem draws full power
# even when the cellular radio is idle.
#
# Fix: enable `wakeup` so the kernel can runtime-suspend the modem
# between cell-tower polls and wake it on incoming traffic. Combined
# with the 500 ms autosuspend_delay the device already advertises,
# this brings runtime_suspended_time from ~13% to >90% in steady-
# state idle, eliminates the per-second xhci interrupt baseline, and
# saves ~0.1-0.2 W continuous draw.
#
# Without this rule the symptom is exactly what we measured on
# 2026-06-30 r281: device at 56 °C battery with all 4 cores idle,
# modem at runtime_status=active 99% of uptime, xhci-hcd:usb1 ticking
# at 36 Hz forever.
#
# Companion to the schedutil governor restoration (PWR-1) — the two
# fixes together are responsible for the bulk of the L5's idle-power
# improvement on Marathon.

SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ATTR{idVendor}=="2020", ATTR{idProduct}=="2060", \
    ATTR{power/wakeup}="enabled", ATTR{power/control}="auto"
